This directory holds a JavaScript command-line library (ES modules; tests run with `node --test`). A program can put its options into named groups in the help output, including the built-in help option. When an application option reuses one of the help option's flags, the help option is shown with only its remaining flag, and in that case it loses its group and appears under the default "Options:" heading.

```js
import { Command, Option } from './index.js';

const program = new Command()
  .option('-h, --host <host>')
  .addHelpOption(new Option('-h, --help', 'display help').helpGroup('Information:'));
console.log(program.helpInformation());
```

This prints `--help` under "Options:". It should print it under "Information:". The same applies when the long flag is the one that is taken: with `program.option('--help <topic>')`, `program.optionsGroup('Information:')` and `program.helpOption(true)`, the remaining `-h` should be listed under "Information:". Help output where no flag conflicts must stay unchanged. Do not edit any existing test file; put new tests in a new file under tests/. The existing suite (`node --test`) must keep passing. Do not ask me questions; if something is unclear, make a reasonable assumption, list your assumptions in your final message, and finish the work.
